# Agent browser spot-checks (CEO account)

**The agent runs post-deploy / parity spot-checks in the browser or via the same auth path the app uses.** Do not ask the CEO to log in and click around unless automation is blocked (captcha, 2FA change, etc.).

## Credentials (never commit)

**Cloud agents:** set in **Cursor Cloud → Secrets** (preferred for cloud-first workflow):

| Variable | Value |
|----------|--------|
| `AGENT_BROWSER_EMAIL` | your test account email (Cursor secret) |
| `AGENT_BROWSER_PASSWORD` | CEO password — dashboard only |

**Local fallback:** same keys in **`.env.local`** at repo root (gitignored).

Pre-flight when script exists:

```bash
npm run agent:browser-auth-check
```

Must print `OK: agent browser credentials valid for <email>`. If the script is missing, verify sign-in manually via API path (Supabase JWT) using env vars above.

## When to spot-check

After deploy or DSC vertical soak when exit tests say "CEO spot-check":

1. **API path (preferred, fast):** Sign in with `.env.local` creds → Supabase `project_steps` read (same RLS as the app). Confirm `step_kind`, tracks, config, status.
2. **Browser path:** `cursor-ide-browser` — log in if needed, open a known test project (see below), open Song/Content/Layout panel, screenshot if useful.

